From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FLOOR Contributors <contributors@floor.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(floor-amm): add FloorAmm (the FLOOR Program) liquidity
 source

One FloorAmm contract per chain; each launch (token vs its quote) trades
against the contract itself from its first block. A launch's state is its
book: the ranges for sale, the floor F, and the bid under the price, the
mirror segments of C and K. The simulator walks that book with a Go port
of the protocol's reference math (math/v2), held to its golden book walks
receipt for receipt (math/v2/testdata, copied verbatim; walkcap.json holds
buys bounded below the 24-step walk, as the protocol's Solana build walks
at most 16 pieces a buy and refunds the rest); the program's
split of a buy's first-time money and its re-lay of C + K are not ported,
so the book after a trade is the walk's, not the program's: after
UpdateBalance the simulator is stale and quotes ErrStaleAfterSwap until
the tracker refreshes it from chain.

- lister: launch ids 1..launchCount(), launchToken / launchQuote; a launch
  whose quote is not listed in the registry (quoteEntry) is held back and
  listed on a later pass once it is (routeUnlisted opts in to all).
- tracker: launchBook(id) and launchFeeCurve(id), one multicall at one
  block (the book's fee is the curve's end rate: pricing needs the curve).
- simulator: exact-in both ways; a buy that the book cannot fill whole
  returns the rest as RemainingTokenAmountIn, a sell takes whole token
  math units (10^-6 token) and returns the rest.
- reserves: F + C + K (the bid money) + the money in place; the tokens the book holds.
- native quote: on Arc the pool's quote token (the wrapped-native entry,
  6 decimals) shares the native coin's balance (18 decimals); amounts are
  rescaled with valueobject.Wrap/UnwrapNativeAmount around the math, as
  uniswap/v4 does. A no-op on every other chain.
